<ul class="pick-specs"><li>Arc-bottom design</li><li>1" and 2" plates</li><li>Harness included</li></ul>
<p><strong>Why it's here:</strong> A lower-cost sled whose curved base glides over grass and turf instead of digging in. It accepts both standard and Olympic plates, which helps if your home weights are a mix.</p><p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Athletes on a budget, parents buying a first sled and anyone training on grass.</p><p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> It's lighter-duty than steel competition sleds, so heavy pushes aren't what it's built for.</p>
